# composer.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. See the "composer.lock" section of
# README.md — a library normally ignores it, and this one does not, because its
# dev dependency tree executes arbitrary code that decides whether the estate's
# authentication gate passes. The cost (CI proving one resolution instead of the
# whole `^12.0|^13.0` range) is paid back by the matrix jobs in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml, which ignore the lock on purpose.
